course: dictionary
lesson: 288
title: Amp: one word, four meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word amp is a good example. In a science lesson it is a unit of electric current. In a music shop it is a machine for louder sound. In slang it can mean excited.
explain: Look at the words around amp. «A fuse is a thin wire that melts if too much current flows, breaking the circuit before the wires overheat; the number on it tells how many amps it allows.» Circuit, current and wires are all about electricity, so amps here is the unit that measures electric current.
explain: Guitarists plug into an amp, and a friend says «The match is on tonight, I'm amped!» Music words and sporting words point to different meanings. Check the clues around the word each time, then swap your meaning into the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
fact: Amp is short for ampere, the unit used to measure electric current. It is written as A.
fact: Current is the flow of electricity. An ammeter is the instrument that measures it in amps.
fact: Amp is also short for amplifier, a machine that makes sound from a guitar or microphone louder.
fact: «Amp up» (slang) means make something stronger or more exciting, and «amped» (slang) means very excited.
fact: The same short word can mean different things in different subjects, so always check the context.
exercise: «A fuse is a thin wire that melts if too much current flows.» On a fuse, what do the amps tell you? | *How many amps it allows | How bright the light will be | How long the fuse will last | How many wires it has
exercise: Jamal says his guitar amp makes his guitar sound much louder. What is an amp in this sentence? | *A machine that makes sound louder | A unit for measuring electric current | A thin wire in a circuit | A kind of guitar string
exercise: Ella says, «Our team is amped for the match!» What does amped mean here? | Very old | Very cold | Very tired | *Very excited
test: In science lessons, electric current is measured in which unit? | Metres | Volts | Grams | *Amps
test: What does «amp up» mean in «They want to amp up the music»? | Measure how long the music lasts | Play it very quietly | *Make the music stronger or more exciting | Turn the music off
exam: «The number on the fuse tells how many amps it allows.» Which instrument measures current in amps? | Set of scales | *Ammeter | Ruler | Thermometer
